WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
- Inside this box is a
stranger's love story.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.732
I shouldn't be doing this.

00:00:05.732 --> 00:00:09.149
(lively, dramatic music)

00:00:10.438 --> 00:00:12.410
One thing you can buy
off of Ebay are people's

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.947
personal, hand-written letters.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:16.172
These are actual letters
that somebody wrote

00:00:16.172 --> 00:00:17.698
to a loved one, or whoever.

00:00:17.698 --> 00:00:21.238
Letters that people never
assumed anyone would read.

00:00:21.238 --> 00:00:24.688
So I saw this set of love letters on Ebay.

00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:27.971
They're from the 1930s,
between two people.

00:00:27.971 --> 00:00:28.804
It was fifty bucks.

00:00:28.804 --> 00:00:29.637
(cash register clings)

00:00:29.637 --> 00:00:30.470
So I bought it.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.303
I got it in the mail.

00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:33.102
And now I have very personal messages

00:00:33.102 --> 00:00:35.910
from two people in the 1930s in love.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.410
(swing music)

00:00:40.529 --> 00:00:42.376
I have no idea who these people were.

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:44.169
These people might be dead at this point.

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:46.219
We're gonna pry into
their personal business.

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:49.790
These letters are all in their
original, stamped envelopes.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.983
Some of these letters are
postmarked only a day apart.

00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:54.965
These people are firing off letters.

00:00:54.965 --> 00:00:57.245
I'm going to change
the names of the people

00:00:57.245 --> 00:00:58.906
to protect their privacies.

00:00:58.906 --> 00:01:00.763
We're going to say that the man is Daniel

00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:02.431
and the woman is Lucy.

00:01:02.431 --> 00:01:03.852
It's not their real names,

00:01:03.852 --> 00:01:05.970
but everything else will
be real from the letters.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:10.002
Opening up someone's
mail feels very wrong.

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:11.692
I'm just like, this is wrong,

00:01:11.692 --> 00:01:13.692
I shouldn't be doing this.

00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:14.950
If you don't want someone

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:17.239
to read your love letters after you die,

00:01:17.239 --> 00:01:19.202
you should burn them,

00:01:19.202 --> 00:01:21.018
or tell your family to burn them.

00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:23.831
Otherwise, someone like me
could read them. (laughs)

00:01:23.831 --> 00:01:25.581
I am one sentence in,

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:29.951
and it's already
completely melted my heart.

00:01:29.951 --> 00:01:30.784
It says.

00:01:30.784 --> 00:01:32.384
- (Lucy) July 14th, 1930.

00:01:32.384 --> 00:01:34.779
I'm home again, and this is
the best thing I've done today,

00:01:34.779 --> 00:01:36.278
write to you.

00:01:36.278 --> 00:01:38.371
I had the blues for a little
while, a few minutes ago,

00:01:38.371 --> 00:01:39.712
but not for long.

00:01:39.712 --> 00:01:41.267
I read your last letter and said,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.396
"Lucy, you certainly ought
to be ashamed of yourself,

00:01:43.396 --> 00:01:44.968
"when Dan has such wonderful faith,

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.704
"and he is the one that's sick."

00:01:46.704 --> 00:01:50.610
- The first thing I've
learned is that Dan is sick.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.137
I was looking at the
postmarks on Dan's letters,

00:01:54.137 --> 00:01:57.259
and I realized that they
came from a hospital.

00:01:57.259 --> 00:01:59.600
So I looked up the hospital,
and it's a hospital

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.400
that was opened in the 1920s
for tuberculosis patients.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.229
So, it's possible that
Dan has tuberculosis.

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:09.089
All we know for sure is that
he's sick and in the hospital.

00:02:09.089 --> 00:02:10.819
The opening to Dan's letter

00:02:10.819 --> 00:02:12.455
is the best thing I've ever read.

00:02:12.455 --> 00:02:14.307
- (Dan) July 30th 1930.

00:02:14.307 --> 00:02:15.455
Honey, honey, honey girl,

00:02:15.455 --> 00:02:17.416
I'm the happiest kid
on Earth this morning,

00:02:17.416 --> 00:02:19.147
and I don't mean maybe.

00:02:19.147 --> 00:02:22.787
- Dan feels like a very
excited, vibrant guy.

00:02:22.787 --> 00:02:24.994
You can definitely tell Dan
has some time on this hands.

00:02:24.994 --> 00:02:26.474
This is long!

00:02:26.474 --> 00:02:28.807
Three pages, front and back.

00:02:29.795 --> 00:02:32.987
I have to say, Dan has
some very fancy stationary.

00:02:32.987 --> 00:02:34.498
This is metallic.

00:02:34.498 --> 00:02:36.241
- (Dan) I love you, my darling.

00:02:36.241 --> 00:02:38.560
And from now on there will be
no more talk of us quitting.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.130
I know it couldn't be done,
and it isn't necessary.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.654
Goodbye, sweetheart.

00:02:42.654 --> 00:02:44.030
All of my love for you.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.360
Your own, Dan.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.250
- This letter talks about how
people have been telling Dan

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.941
he should break up with
Lucy because he's sick,

00:02:52.941 --> 00:02:55.171
and he shouldn't be in a relationship

00:02:55.171 --> 00:02:56.462
while he's sick, basically.

00:02:56.462 --> 00:02:57.750
Dan is very excited because

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.590
one of the staff members at the hospital

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.518
said he should not break up with Lucy.

00:03:01.518 --> 00:03:03.542
That Lucy is a really good girlfriend

00:03:03.542 --> 00:03:05.139
who's helping him get better.

00:03:05.139 --> 00:03:06.891
It's crazy to hold up this piece of paper

00:03:06.891 --> 00:03:09.742
and know that it was written
more than 80 years ago.

00:03:09.742 --> 00:03:11.342
I'm starting to realize
that they've written

00:03:11.342 --> 00:03:13.040
so many letters to each other

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.330
because Daniel is stuck in a sanatorium,

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.640
and they have to be apart.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.451
- (Lucy) August 7th 1930.

00:03:19.451 --> 00:03:21.440
Dan darling, sometimes I
feel a little bit afraid

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.142
because we love each other so much.

00:03:23.142 --> 00:03:26.131
If anything should happen,
but that's silly, I know.

00:03:26.131 --> 00:03:27.472
- I mean, obviously
Lucy doesn't want to say

00:03:27.472 --> 00:03:30.174
she's scared Dan will die.

00:03:30.174 --> 00:03:33.603
But you can tell she's still
very worried about him.

00:03:33.603 --> 00:03:36.003
And at this point we
don't know how sick he is.

00:03:36.003 --> 00:03:37.974
And we don't know if this is

00:03:37.974 --> 00:03:39.574
like a life-or-death situation or not.

00:03:39.574 --> 00:03:41.232
Reading one of Lucy's latest letters,

00:03:41.232 --> 00:03:44.334
it sounds like she's
studying to be a nurse.

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.464
So she might be college age.

00:03:46.464 --> 00:03:48.032
She might be in her late teens.

00:03:48.032 --> 00:03:50.712
But she also talks about being young.

00:03:50.712 --> 00:03:53.594
Like, she feels like she's
not yet a young lady.

00:03:53.594 --> 00:03:57.519
I'm four letters in, and we
finally got to some sex stuff.

00:03:57.519 --> 00:03:58.992
It sounds like Dan had

00:03:58.992 --> 00:04:03.203
some kind of sexual dream
that he told Lucy about.

00:04:03.203 --> 00:04:05.563
Unfortunately, I don't have that letter.

00:04:05.563 --> 00:04:08.563
But I do have Lucy's response.

00:04:08.563 --> 00:04:10.573
- (Lucy) September 23rd, 1930.

00:04:10.573 --> 00:04:12.872
My sweetheart, you surely
did have a funny dream.

00:04:12.872 --> 00:04:14.944
Well, I can't tell you
just how I would act

00:04:14.944 --> 00:04:16.292
under such circumstances.

00:04:16.292 --> 00:04:17.704
You see, darling,

00:04:17.704 --> 00:04:19.333
I really haven't had much experience

00:04:19.333 --> 00:04:21.503
with gentlemen who do things
like you did in your dream.

00:04:21.503 --> 00:04:22.752
That's right, I'm not a blonde!

00:04:22.752 --> 00:04:25.926
So one could hardly expect
you to be a gentleman.

00:04:25.926 --> 00:04:27.232
But I always wear pjs, Dan.

00:04:27.232 --> 00:04:28.065
Always!

00:04:28.065 --> 00:04:30.843
However, I just love trying new things,

00:04:30.843 --> 00:04:32.894
and with sufficient inducement.

00:04:32.894 --> 00:04:35.752
- Lucy talks about Dan wanting something

00:04:35.752 --> 00:04:40.752
that she can't give him
yet, until they get married.

00:04:40.835 --> 00:04:43.664
And I have a feeling
that that things is sex.

00:04:43.664 --> 00:04:47.623
It's not clear, but that's my best guess.

00:04:47.623 --> 00:04:49.581
- (Lucy) October 2nd, 1930.

00:04:49.581 --> 00:04:52.130
Here I am in my little bed,
in the little pink room,

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.480
just wishing so hard that
you were here with me.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.890
I surely hope that you
don't get much thinner.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.210
It makes me feel terrible
to see you like that.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.730
And I guess it's my fault.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.519
Darling, I hadn't thought of that

00:05:02.519 --> 00:05:03.741
before you told me yesterday.

00:05:03.741 --> 00:05:06.341
I do love you so much, Dan darling.

00:05:06.341 --> 00:05:08.560
I'd surely like to give you what you want,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.152
and I want it, too.

00:05:10.152 --> 00:05:12.290
But there's no use to
think of it right now.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.880
Sweetheart, I hope that we
can be married next summer.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.952
So you'll try real hard to
be patient, won't you, Dan?

00:05:17.952 --> 00:05:20.877
- (Dan) January 22nd, 1931.

00:05:20.877 --> 00:05:23.290
My own little sweetheart,
I need you tonight

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.032
because I'm as lonely as can be.

00:05:25.032 --> 00:05:26.399
I'd like to crawl into your arms

00:05:26.399 --> 00:05:27.925
and be your little boy tonight.

00:05:27.925 --> 00:05:30.312
I'm just blue and need to be comforted.

00:05:30.312 --> 00:05:32.141
I'll always need you, darling girl.

00:05:32.141 --> 00:05:33.204
But just now it seems

00:05:33.204 --> 00:05:35.270
like I'll go crazy if
I can't have you soon.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:36.620
Oh, Lucy, my sweetheart.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.471
I shouldn't be begging you all the time,

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:39.881
but I can't help it.

00:05:39.881 --> 00:05:43.012
- So Dan sent pretty much an entire letter

00:05:43.012 --> 00:05:45.156
about how he wants to go to the bone zone.

00:05:45.156 --> 00:05:46.684
With Lucy.

00:05:46.684 --> 00:05:48.374
- (Dan) March 13th, 1931.

00:05:48.374 --> 00:05:50.744
I like to tease you a little
bit about certain things,

00:05:50.744 --> 00:05:52.452
because you're so funny, sweet about it.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.848
You're just a darling
baby girl, my sweetness.

00:05:54.848 --> 00:05:56.538
You don't mind if I
talk that way sometimes.

00:05:56.538 --> 00:05:57.371
Do you?

00:05:57.371 --> 00:05:59.381
As a matter of fact,
I think you'd like it,

00:05:59.381 --> 00:06:01.299
just as you'd like what I talk about.

00:06:01.299 --> 00:06:03.601
Anyway, I'll promise
what you asked me, honey,

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.700
and I won't really try to do what I said.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.635
Although if it happens, I can't help it.

00:06:07.635 --> 00:06:08.499
Can I?

00:06:08.499 --> 00:06:09.851
And I kinda hope it does,

00:06:09.851 --> 00:06:12.419
'cause I'll surely like to have
another baby girl like you.

00:06:12.419 --> 00:06:14.486
- I just feel like, if
you're a woman 80 years ago,

00:06:14.486 --> 00:06:17.177
dating had to be so stressful.

00:06:17.177 --> 00:06:18.360
Your only options are,

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.849
wait until you're married to have sex,

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:23.266
or roll the dice.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.829
Because birth control
options were very limited.

00:06:27.829 --> 00:06:29.891
Abortions were illegal.

00:06:29.891 --> 00:06:33.949
Having a child outside of
marriage was pretty frowned upon.

00:06:33.949 --> 00:06:35.811
You didn't have a lot of options.

00:06:35.811 --> 00:06:38.249
And if your boyfriend in the hospital

00:06:38.249 --> 00:06:40.462
is pressuring you to have sex,

00:06:40.462 --> 00:06:41.971
you know, I feel for Lucy.

00:06:41.971 --> 00:06:44.171
- (Lucy) March 30th, 1931.

00:06:44.171 --> 00:06:45.760
Do you know what I love to think about?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.622
It's the time when you'll be well,

00:06:47.622 --> 00:06:49.400
and we can do things together.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.731
That will be so nice.

00:06:50.731 --> 00:06:54.948
- At this point, Dan has been
in the hospital for months.

00:06:54.948 --> 00:06:56.851
It sounds like they can
only spend time together

00:06:56.851 --> 00:06:59.640
when Lucy comes to visit the hospital.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.870
She obviously wants to
visit as much as she can,

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:02.950
but she's gotta work.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.451
She's got a life to live.

00:07:04.451 --> 00:07:06.461
And it sounds like it's really hard.

00:07:06.461 --> 00:07:08.280
- (Lucy) March 31st 1931.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:11.299
I wish that I could kiss you
now, my own darling lover.

00:07:11.299 --> 00:07:13.150
Although it might never
make any difference.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.291
It's rather risky.

00:07:14.291 --> 00:07:16.419
- We don't know what Dan is sick with.

00:07:16.419 --> 00:07:19.459
He might have tuberculosis,
and that is contagious.

00:07:19.459 --> 00:07:20.399
I actually Googled,

00:07:20.399 --> 00:07:21.232
(keyboard typing)

00:07:21.232 --> 00:07:23.871
"Can you get tuberculosis from kissing?"

00:07:23.871 --> 00:07:27.128
And it turns out, you can't
get tuberculosis from kissing.

00:07:27.128 --> 00:07:28.396
Or sex.

00:07:28.396 --> 00:07:30.528
That's great news for Lucy and Dan.

00:07:30.528 --> 00:07:32.567
- (Lucy) April 10th, 1931.

00:07:32.567 --> 00:07:33.712
Honey boy o' mine.

00:07:33.712 --> 00:07:35.294
Wouldn't it be fun if we could have

00:07:35.294 --> 00:07:37.569
a little cottage in the
desert or in the hills?

00:07:37.569 --> 00:07:39.830
And just be there together all the time?

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:41.845
Sweetheart, that would be wonderful.

00:07:41.845 --> 00:07:43.447
But too good to be true, I guess.

00:07:43.447 --> 00:07:45.516
- (Dan) June 16th, 1931.

00:07:45.516 --> 00:07:47.567
Something tell me that our day is coming.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:48.926
We're gonna have our little house,

00:07:48.926 --> 00:07:50.698
and just be happy having each other,

00:07:50.698 --> 00:07:52.498
and we'll do lots of
things that will be fun.

00:07:52.498 --> 00:07:54.412
We can play and work together.

00:07:54.412 --> 00:07:55.545
Read nice books.

00:07:55.545 --> 00:07:56.378
Listen to music.

00:07:56.378 --> 00:07:57.999
Take long walks and rides together.

00:07:57.999 --> 00:08:00.577
And, always, we can have
our lovin' every day.

00:08:00.577 --> 00:08:01.567
And every night.

00:08:01.567 --> 00:08:03.007
Well, that's paradise.

00:08:03.007 --> 00:08:05.079
- Dan, he's coming from this place

00:08:05.079 --> 00:08:07.162
of extreme, deep yearning

00:08:08.039 --> 00:08:10.679
for these things that are just so simple,

00:08:10.679 --> 00:08:14.186
as like reading a book
with his girlfriend.

00:08:14.186 --> 00:08:15.925
You have to appreciate the little things.

00:08:15.925 --> 00:08:17.087
Dan does.

00:08:17.087 --> 00:08:19.185
- (Dan) June 30th, 1931.

00:08:19.185 --> 00:08:20.340
I'm anxious to get a letter today

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.152
so I'll know what you found out Monday.

00:08:22.152 --> 00:08:23.654
Gee, I hope everything is alright.

00:08:23.654 --> 00:08:26.163
Honey, I wish I could have
gone to the doctor with you.

00:08:26.163 --> 00:08:28.492
It doesn't seem right to send you alone.

00:08:28.492 --> 00:08:29.534
It isn't right.

00:08:29.534 --> 00:08:31.174
Gee, honey, I hope it isn't necessary

00:08:31.174 --> 00:08:32.743
for you to go through a lot of trouble.

00:08:32.743 --> 00:08:33.713
You weren't meant for trouble

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:35.522
and I'm sorry if I got
you in for a lot of it.

00:08:35.522 --> 00:08:37.374
Honey, I guess I'm an awful, dumb guy,

00:08:37.374 --> 00:08:39.243
but I'm sure glad you love me anyway.

00:08:39.243 --> 00:08:41.225
- So I guess I should not be surprised

00:08:41.225 --> 00:08:44.233
This letter from Dan insinuates

00:08:44.233 --> 00:08:47.134
that he may have gotten Lucy pregnant,

00:08:47.134 --> 00:08:50.471
and she has to go to
the doctor and find out.

00:08:50.471 --> 00:08:53.533
Sounds like they may have gone
to the bone zone after all.

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.757
But then, there's no more
letters from Lucy left.

00:08:55.757 --> 00:08:58.065
It's all letters from Dan.

00:08:58.065 --> 00:09:00.275
I'm not even gonna hear from Lucy again

00:09:00.275 --> 00:09:02.155
about whether or not she's pregnant.

00:09:02.155 --> 00:09:02.988
Ahah!

00:09:04.145 --> 00:09:05.862
- (Dan) August 8th 1931.

00:09:05.862 --> 00:09:06.846
Just think, honey.

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:08.531
You'll be Mama, and I'll be Papa!

00:09:08.531 --> 00:09:09.364
Aint that something?

00:09:09.364 --> 00:09:10.767
You're my wonderful treasure.

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:13.277
You and a tiny bit of
little precious treasure

00:09:13.277 --> 00:09:14.208
that belongs to us.

00:09:14.208 --> 00:09:16.997
- I have four more letters to go,

00:09:16.997 --> 00:09:19.088
and I'm just trying to
read them as fast as I can,

00:09:19.088 --> 00:09:20.616
because I am dying to know

00:09:20.616 --> 00:09:23.128
what happens to Lucy and Dan.

00:09:23.128 --> 00:09:25.797
And, I hope Lucy's okay.

00:09:25.797 --> 00:09:27.637
And I hope that they can be together.

00:09:27.637 --> 00:09:29.629
They just want to start a little family

00:09:29.629 --> 00:09:31.938
and live in a little house together.

00:09:31.938 --> 00:09:33.955
Is that so much to ask?

00:09:33.955 --> 00:09:35.829
- (Dan) August 19th, 1931.

00:09:35.829 --> 00:09:37.988
Say, sweetheart, we're going to have

00:09:37.988 --> 00:09:40.122
the best honeymoon of all time, aren't we?

00:09:40.122 --> 00:09:41.869
Just being together will
be a great treat for us.

00:09:41.869 --> 00:09:44.357
Honey, I want you to take
Hubbard's scrapbook along.

00:09:44.357 --> 00:09:46.697
And that book of poems
you gave me at Christmas.

00:09:46.697 --> 00:09:48.167
And any other books you think of.

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:50.036
Don't you think that would be nice?

00:09:50.036 --> 00:09:51.966
Maybe we'll be too busy to look at them.

00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:53.216
But I don't know,

00:09:53.216 --> 00:09:54.825
I've never been on a honeymoon before.

00:09:54.825 --> 00:09:55.658
(cheerful swing music)

00:09:55.658 --> 00:09:56.920
I hope that both of us are
feeling good at that time.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.848
But I know that I'll have to stick

00:09:58.848 --> 00:10:00.349
pretty close to bed until then.

00:10:00.349 --> 00:10:02.389
Else, I might not even be able to go.

00:10:02.389 --> 00:10:04.539
- We're going to see what
this last letter has to say.

00:10:04.539 --> 00:10:09.469
I'm nervous because I'm worried
I will be lacking in closure

00:10:09.469 --> 00:10:11.379
about what happens to Lucy and Dan.

00:10:11.379 --> 00:10:13.789
- (Dan) October 21st, 1931.

00:10:13.789 --> 00:10:16.429
I can't think of anything but
you and our baby and our home.

00:10:16.429 --> 00:10:17.599
Oh, my sweetheart.

00:10:17.599 --> 00:10:18.818
I do love you so much.

00:10:18.818 --> 00:10:21.149
You're my very own precious little wifey.

00:10:21.149 --> 00:10:22.847
All of my love for you, always.

00:10:22.847 --> 00:10:24.128
Your own, Dan.

00:10:24.128 --> 00:10:27.238
- Dan and Lucy are preparing
to move in together,

00:10:27.238 --> 00:10:28.889
in their own place.

00:10:28.889 --> 00:10:30.512
That's what they've always dreamed of.

00:10:30.512 --> 00:10:33.433
Unfortunately, Dan is still sick,

00:10:33.433 --> 00:10:34.764
and I'm still really wondering

00:10:34.764 --> 00:10:36.444
how Lucy feels about all this.

00:10:36.444 --> 00:10:38.461
And how her pregnancy is going.

00:10:38.461 --> 00:10:40.132
But I guess we'll never know.

00:10:40.132 --> 00:10:43.473
Maybe their child is out there, somewhere.

00:10:43.473 --> 00:10:45.132
(baby crying)

00:10:45.132 --> 00:10:46.724
Reading the mail of total strangers,

00:10:46.724 --> 00:10:49.312
mostly just made me feel really grateful.

00:10:49.312 --> 00:10:51.612
Grateful for health.

00:10:51.612 --> 00:10:53.812
Grateful that modern birth control exists.

00:10:53.812 --> 00:10:56.713
Grateful to know the phrase "honey-man"

00:10:56.713 --> 00:10:58.873
as a term of endearment

00:10:58.873 --> 00:11:00.284
that I'm going to start calling everyone.

00:11:00.284 --> 00:11:03.367
(slow soulful music)

